st dose and 76 had  received the second dose as well and he  also talked about teenagers people  between the ages of 15 and 18 and said  10 million of them had got birth doses  so india is doing pretty well in terms  of vaccination as you said over a  billion people to be vaccinated and to  get that number as high as that is quite  a a significant achievement i mean that  95 percent is better than germany and  now we've seen mass gatherings like  religious festivals and political  rallies drive new surges in the country  and i know we have a big regional  election getting underway in uttar  pradesh it's a state with 200 million  people i'm curious have there been steps  taken to control crowd sizes there  in fact uttar pradesh has a population  which is half the size of the european  union so elections which started there  today are going to go on for a month in  seven phases the election  commission gave guidelines as to how  these  rallies and campaigns could take place  but of course no one is paying any  attention the election commission said  not more than 50 capacity in indoor  auditoriums and not more than 30 percent  outdoors they said only 20 percent at  two so i beg your pardon only 20 people  were allowed to go for door-to-door  campaigns they put a bar on rallies  processions and so on but if you look at  the pictures you will see that no one's  paying any attention to these guidelines  many thousands and thousands of people  are out at these rallies there's no  social distancing hardly anyone is  wearing a mask not even the politicians  so we'll just have to wait and see  melissa what happens after these  elections are over in a month or so  because last time in a similar situation  when there were regional elections in  india we saw a huge spike in the number  of new infections  dw's delhi bureau chief amita chima  thank you for that roundup  [Music]  turning now to the challenge of long  covid which some now call the parallel  pandemic  estimates suggest more than a third of  covid survivors will develop symptoms  that linger long past the initial  infection they can range from headaches  to fatigue and also to more serious  conditions we take a closer look at this  from india where dw's menier chaudhry  reports  sadhna tandon calls her pet dog pepper  her lifeline  she says the pup keeps her on her toes  all day  something which she says was not  possible just a couple of months ago  63 year old sadhna was infected with the  coronavirus during the second wave while  her initial infection was not severe a  few days after testing negative she was  diagnosed with cardiac inflammation a  post covert complication which left her  with a crippling weakness for months i  used to feel so weak so weak that i  would at times used to feel like i can't  even sit i must lie down i hardly had  any stamina i was though a very active  person earlier  and i started feeling depressed also i  used to feel it very low sadhna's case  is not exceptional  many other people have suffered from  post covert complaints  more commonly known as long covet  a name given to the persistent illness a  person feels while facing symptoms or  effects for weeks or months after  testing negative for the coronavirus  dr ayush gupta says patients have come  to him with complications like headache  fatigue depression palpitations and  cardiac issues among others a staggering  number that is 60 to 70 percent of  patients who recover from covid  have these effects on them there are  some kind of risk factors which predict  long covet duration of illness is one  severity of illness is second it is not  completely understood it is a science in  evolution so even young patients may be  experiencing more symptoms than an  elderly high risk patient  30 year old roshni divakar was an avid  yoga practitioner  she says she was at her healthiest stage  when she tested positive during the  second wave and her infection was quite  mild  but soon after she started experiencing  complications and was diagnosed with a  balanced disorder called vestibular  disorder which makes her feel dizzy and  causes constant ringing in her ears it's  like being on a boat  all the time  so when i stand it the floor is like  this so for me to walk straight is a  struggle there was a point where i  literally needed to be lifted to go  anywhere because i just couldn't get my  balance it can be very overwhelming and  exhausting while for roshni it has been  rehabilitative therapy and yoga that  have helped her gain a sense of control  over her condition for sadhana it's been  medication ample rest and her pepper  which helped her with her post-covet  complication he sleeps with me he eats  with me like a small child i have a  grandchild home now  [Laughter]  sadhna says she is a lot better now as  she has found some happy distraction  with pepper  but for many like her the lingering  effect of kovid remains inexplicable
 

